      "content": "Progress looks good, but I'm looking at the projected coverage maps for after the Alpha-6 thru Alpha-12 units go offline. It looks like the decommissioning is going to create some massive latency spikes and signal dead zones over the North Atlantic and parts of Europe. The current plan is to just let those gaps happen and re-route everything through the Beta plane, but the bandwidth overhead is going to be huge. \n\nCan you run a quick simulation on how much the network stability will drop once those units are actually taken out of rotation?",
